What Is the CMP Slurry Market?
Chemical Mechanical Planarization (CMP) slurry is a specialized consumable used in semiconductor manufacturing to achieve smooth and uniform wafer surfaces. It combines abrasive particles, such as silica or ceria, with chemical additives, pH regulators, and dispersants.

The slurry performs simultaneous chemical and mechanical material removal during wafer polishing. It is used in dielectric, metal, barrier, and other specialized planarization processes, helping prepare wafer surfaces for subsequent lithography, deposition, and interconnect manufacturing steps.

